{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This is an on-demand trip — scheduled_at is null — so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait runs from the driver's arrival, not from any schedule. The trip record shows the driver marking arrived at 13:11:50, the free-wait timer starting at 13:11:55 and expiring at 13:16:55, and the cancellation at 13:18:20: 390 s after arrival, 90 s past the end of the free wait. On those timings the driver cancelled only after the wait had fully run, which is exactly what POL-NS-21 permits.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 voids the fee only where the driver failed to message AND call before cancelling. Both limbs are satisfied on the COMPLETE records: the chat log carries two in-app messages sent by the driver, at 13:12:10 and 13:15:00, and the trip record carries an in-app call placed by the driver at 13:14:20 — all three before the 13:18:20 cancellation. The clause requires a call to be placed, not answered, so the 20 s unanswered ring-out satisfies it. The contact obligation is met and there is no ground to void the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06061", "EV-TRIP-06061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The payments ledger shows exactly 5.00 SGD charged for the cancellation — the policy fee — with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so nothing has yet moved. Under POL-NS-22, where the free wait has run and the fee stands, the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both equal to the fee charged, 5.00 SGD; POL-GEN-03 confirms that figure is the money the ruling moves, not a second payment.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-06061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.fee_charged_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No FULL_REFUND is available to the rider on this record. On a no-show charge only POL-NS-23 and POL-NS-24 favour the rider, and both fail: the contact obligation was met (POL-NS-23), and POL-NS-24 needs a scheduled pickup time the driver missed by five minutes, but this trip is on-demand with scheduled_at null, so there is no scheduled time to miss and no deadline to fix. The rider's 'he never came' account therefore has no refund clause to stand on, and the present charge must be left intact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06061", "EV-CHAT-06061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.scheduled_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose rather than hide the state of the trace: the GPS artifact is IMPAIRED, weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION, and its derived arrival check reports corroborated false with nearest_fix null. It cannot be presented as clean corroboration. But a 640 s gap is absent data, not evidence that the driver was somewhere else, and the arrival event, the 'driver has arrived' push notification to the rider at 13:11:54 and the free-wait timer are all carried independently on the COMPLETE trip record at weight 1.0. The impairment caps the weight of the trace; it does not erase the platform record of arrival.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-06061", "EV-TRIP-06061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check.corroborated",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the most sceptical reading of the impaired trace — that the arrival is not GPS-corroborated — the result is not a refund. POL-GEN-26 sends a case to human review precisely where a needed fact (here, when the driver arrived) cannot be established on impaired evidence, and on escalation the amount is held, not returned. That is the floor of this case, and it still leaves the 5.00 SGD with the driver rather than the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-06061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case turns on one fact — whether the driver was actually at Block 14, Eunos Crescent, and when — because the 5.00 SGD no-show fee depends on a 5-minute free wait that can only start once he is there. On this record that fact cannot be established, so the case goes to a human reviewer and the 5.00 SGD is held: it is neither refunded to the rider nor paid out to the driver for now.\n\nWHY THE ARRIVAL IS UNDECIDED. The category's arrival test treats the driver as at the pickup only when the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace inside 50 m and a 120 s window. EV-GPS-06061 reports corroborated = false and nearest_fix = null. That trace is impaired: weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION — a single 640 s gap from 13:08:50 to 13:19:30 that swallows the 13:11:50 arrival marker, the whole free-wait window (13:11:50–13:16:50) and the 13:18:20 cancellation, with coverage at 28.6% (8 fixes against a 30 s interval). POL-NS-08(b) makes a gap longer than 120 s inside the waiting window a policy-level impairment, and the test here has no fix inside the window it reads at all.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CASE (POL-NS-21, POL-NS-22, POL-GEN-02). You are right that on an on-demand trip the free wait runs from arrival, and that 390 s from the arrival marker to the cancellation is 90 s past the end of it. But the marker you measure from is the driver's own \"arrived\" tap, and a status a party sets records only that the party set it; the 13:11:54 \"driver has arrived\" push and the 13:11:55 wait timer are platform records of that same tap and do not independently establish presence. The chat messages (\"Reached Blk 14 drop off\" 13:12:10, \"Waiting\" 13:15:00) and the counterparty statement (\"I was there\") are accounts offered in place of a GPS reading the test admits none of, so they do not stand in for it. The arrival is therefore not made out, and DRIVER_COMPENSATION at 5.00 SGD under POL-NS-22 cannot issue. I have disclosed EV-GPS-06061, its weight and its issue code as POL-GEN-02(1) requires.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CASE (POL-NS-21, POL-GEN-26, POL-NS-24, POL-GEN-03). The same impairment cuts the other way. An undecided limb supports neither a payment that needs the clause to hold nor a refund that needs it to fail, so the fee is not voided either and FULL_REFUND of the 5.00 SGD is not available. Your money point is accurate on the figures — EV-FARE-06061 shows cancellation_fee 5.00, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, with refund_if_voided_sgd 5.00 — but the money is not the issue; the arrival is. On POL-NS-24, the driver no-show clause, this trip is on-demand with scheduled_at null, so there is no scheduled time to miss and no deadline to fix; as that clause's own note says, where the record carries none and the deadline cannot be fixed, POL-GEN-26 applies — which is where we land, by escalation rather than by a refund.\n\nWHAT DECIDES IT. POL-GEN-26: where a fact a rule of this version needs — here, when the driver arrived, and so whether the free wait ever began — cannot be established because the evidence that would carry it is impaired, the case is escalated and the open question is stated. The open question for the reviewer is when, and whether, the driver was at Block 14 between roughly 13:09 and 13:19:30, the stretch the trace leaves unobserved.\n\nCONTACT OBLIGATION (POL-NS-23) — NOT A GROUND FOR REFUND. EV-CHAT-06061 (complete, weight 1.0) shows two driver messages at 13:12:10 and 13:15:00, and EV-TRIP-06061 shows one in-app call placed at 13:14:20, all before the 13:18:20 cancellation; the clause requires a call to be placed, not answered, so the 20 s unanswered ring meets it. Both sides accept this limb is met, and it voids nothing.\n\nNO REFERRAL FIRES. The fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not apply; rider_profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d count at or above 3, so POL-NS-25 does not apply; and POL-NS-24's goodwill credit needs the driver to have both failed to arrive and failed to attempt contact, and contact was in fact attempted. The 5.00 SGD is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nCONFIDENCE. 0.6, capped by EV-GPS-06061 (weight 0.6) — the impaired artifact the escalation rests on. POL-NS-26 and POL-GEN-22 require no higher bar for a no-show below 10.00 SGD with no fraud or safety flag."
  },
