    "explanation": "This dispute is about the 5.00 SGD no-show fee on trip TRP-06061 (EV-FARE-06061: cancellation_fee 5.00 SGD, total_charged 5.00 SGD, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, payment_status CHARGED). The rider says the driver never came to Block 14; the driver says he was there. The whole case turns on one fact: whether the driver was physically at the pickup, because on this on-demand trip (scheduled_at null) the 300 s free wait that POL-NS-21 requires runs from the driver's arrival.\n\nUnder this category's arrival test, the driver is at the pickup only when the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace inside a 50 m radius (STANDARD). That trace, EV-GPS-06061, is IMPAIRED: issue code GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION, weight_multiplier 0.6. It carries a single 640 s gap from 13:08:50 to 13:19:30 that swallows the 13:11:50 arrival marker, the entire free-wait window and the 13:18:20 cancellation; its own derived arrival check returns corroborated = false with nearest_fix = null, and there is no fix at all inside the window. The 13:11:50 'driver arrived' entry is an arrival tap — a status the driver set — and the driver's chat messages ('Reached Blk 14 drop off', 13:12:10; 'Waiting', 13:15:00) and his counterparty statement ('I was there') only re-assert what the impaired trace cannot check: they stand in for the test exactly where it admitted no reading, so they neither carry the arrival nor lift the 0.6 cap.\n\nThat leaves the arrival — and with it the free-wait start the fee depends on — undecided, and an undecided limb supports neither the payment the driver claims nor the refund the rider seeks. POL-GEN-26 is directly on point: where a fact a rule needs (here, when the driver arrived) cannot be established because the evidence that would carry it is impaired, the case is escalated and the open question stated. The 5.00 SGD is therefore held, neither collected nor refunded.\n\nOn the points both sides agree: the contact obligation is met. EV-CHAT-06061 (COMPLETE) shows the driver's two in-app messages and EV-TRIP-06061 shows his in-app call at 13:14:20, all before the 13:18:20 cancellation, so POL-NS-23 does not void the fee and no FULL_REFUND arises on that limb. POL-NS-24 gives no refund either — this on-demand trip has no scheduled pickup time, so none was missed. The driver's POL-NS-22 claim for DRIVER_COMPENSATION fails because the free-wait precondition it needs is precisely the limb left undecided (the 390 s is measured from the uncorroborated arrival tap, not from an established arrival). No POL-NS-24 goodwill credit arises, since contact was attempted, and the fee charged equals the 5.00 SGD policy fee, so no POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral fires. Confidence is capped at 0.6, the weight of the impaired GPS artifact that carries the deciding fact (POL-GEN-02(2)).\n\nOpen question for the human reviewer: establish whether the driver was physically at Block 14, Eunos Crescent at about 13:11:50 on 2026-10-04 — e.g. from vehicle telemetry or another independent record — and so whether the 300 s free wait validly ran before the 13:18:20 no-show cancellation. Until that is resolved the 5.00 SGD stays held."
